license: "CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0"
abstract: >-
  Scarce capacity systems such as ports, spectrum, hospital beds, and compute still allocate by first-come-first-served or crude auctions that reward booking bursts and ignore stability under oversubscription. We propose INTENTIDE: a collective intent stability protocol with Synchronization Stress Index, revise-or-confirm rounds, and stability-weighted fair reservation with deterministic settlement digests. This Public Research Edition (v1.3.0) packages an importable research library (from intentide import INTENTIDEEngine), Reality Gate and benchmark PASS evidence, mutation testing, alternative implementation replication, an eighty-carrier fifteen-slot cold-storage port scenario with dropout, demand-spike, and partial-capacity edge cases, stress tests to 5,000 agents at ten-to-one oversubscription with sampled coalition checks, standards mapping to DMA fairness themes, IMO FAL, and ISO 22301, deployment manifests, competitive positioning against FCFS, auctions, and schedulers, and an honest gap register. INTENTIDE is not a live terminal operating system and does not claim mechanism-design completeness against strategic gaming. This independent technical blueprint does not claim peer review, independent human replication, patentability, or legal compliance opinion. It is released for evaluation, citation, and attempted falsification.
